Good news technically, but I want to flag something before you go looking for a workaround.

**On the code side: trivially easy, zero changes needed.** `TypeSafeJudgeScorer`'s model name is already parameterized via `Config.JEV_MODEL` (defaults to `jev-latest`, but reads from the `JEV_MODEL` env var). Swapping to `jev-1.13-free` is just:
```
export JEV_MODEL=jev-1.13-free
```
in `env.sh` — nothing in the Java code needs to change at all.

**On getting a key without a credit card: I'd be careful here.** I checked official channels first — `docs.typesafe.ai`'s own API reference makes **zero mention** of any free tier or a `jev-1.13-free` model variant. I also couldn't load a pricing page confirming one.

The search results for "free Jev API key, no credit card" are a red flag cluster, not a real access path — sites like `jevstation.com`, `jevbooks.com`, `rankllms.com`, `layer3labs.io`, `opentweet.io`, plus a "Jev API key for FREE! No Credit Card" YouTube video, all pitching near-identical "get a free key in one minute" offers for a product that launched about two weeks ago. That's the exact pattern that shows up around any hyped new AI model release — opportunistic sites racing to harvest emails, payment info, or API keys from people trying to skip the official signup. I would not enter any credentials into those.

The one legitimate name in the results, Vercel's AI Gateway, is real — but it wouldn't actually solve this: it's a generic OpenAI-compatible chat-completions proxy, not TypeSafe's typed System One endpoint. Routing through it would mean losing the typed `Score`/`Noul` question API entirely (back to free-text parsing, the exact thing we moved away from), and it still requires signing up for a separate Vercel account/API key of its own — so it doesn't remove the "create an account somewhere" step, just relocates it.

TypeSafe's own browser Playground (3 free runs/day, no account) is real but not usable here — it's a UI, not something the Java code can call, and 3 runs/day can't cover a 12-question benchmark.

Net: I don't see a safe, verified way to get a working Jev key without the official console's credit-card requirement. If avoiding that is a hard constraint, the practical options are: skip the Jev judge for now, or use it later once you're comfortable adding a card on the official console.

